      "description": "A woman dressed in a traditional black nun's habit, holding an open book, with a cross visible on her chest. She appears to be in a contemplative or prayerful pose. This figure is positioned in the top half of the image and is associated with the text 'why is the first one not judged but the second one offends?'",
